CM_ "Reference DBC for the legacy Model 3/Y, not loaded by the apps (they load the smaller vehicles/tesla/bus_1_tesla_vehicle.dbc, which this file extends with the messages of more than 64 signals and the ones the test car never sent). Both DashKit buses. Messages DashPilot reads are unchanged, except DI_speed (full layout). The others were checked against full-bus recordings of a 2023 Model Y RWD (78 min, 2026-11-20): where the ESP32-DualCAN project's definition (Model3_CH.dbc / Model3_VEH.dbc, github.com/dzid26, CERN-OHL-W v2; see each message comment) decodes more of the car's frames with no unexplained bit, it replaces the earlier one, and messages the file lacked were added below this line. An id that is a different message on each bus has the definition that fits more frames. A name the car uses for two ids has the id as a suffix on the second. UNK_ messages: seen on the car, no public definition. Messages whose comment says they were not seen were never sent by the test car (other drive units, charging, options): they are included unchecked, for other legacy Model 3/Y.";

